{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-258861-r4513969","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Bison à la Grecque","sourcePageId":258861,"sourceRevision":"4513969","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:42:30Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Bison%20%C3%A0%20la%20Grecque&oldid=4513969","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:43.580Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using bison","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using cream","Category:Recipes using fennel bulb","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using lemon","Category:Recipes using veal broth and stock","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b25fbdffeb580084902341c9ba844b2ac99c088ef9caecfa999a925af4d3b0c4","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Bison à la Grecque.jpg|300px]]\n}}{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Bison à la grecque''' is a campfire fusion recipe for bison served with a velouté inspired by Mediterranean cuisine.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lbs]] [[Cookbook:Bison|bison]] steak or roast\n* 2 small [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], halved\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]] stalk, [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]], sliced\n* 1 small green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], sliced\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Fennel|fennel]] bulb, sliced\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] clove, crushed\n* 15 [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seeds\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] melted bison fat\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Veal|veal]] [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]], halved\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* ¼ cup dry white [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Brown vegetables in bison fat in a cast iron [[Cookbook:Dutch Oven|Dutch oven]].\n# Add bison, coriander, garlic, bay leaf, veal stock, and lemon. Cover and [[Cookbook:Braising|braise]] over a low fire 2–3 hours or longer until tender.\n# Remove bison to serving tray near fire. Strain sauce into separate bowl, and discard pulp.\n# Make a [[Cookbook:Roux|roux]] in the Dutch oven with butter and flour. Stir in wine and cream, and cook until bubbly. Stir in reserved sauce until thickened, adding more liquid as needed.\n# Season velouté to taste. Pour over bison.\n# Serve with toasted bread, wild mushrooms, and wild rice.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using bison]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]\n[[fr:Livre de cuisine/Bison à la grecque]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fennel bulb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Cate